{"uid":"utils/padding.py","name":"padding.py","qualname":"utils/padding.py","kind":"module","file":"utils/padding.py","line":1,"end_line":225,"language":"py","signature":"","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"Fixed-bucket padding for metadata-size concealment (QV-PAD-1).","description":"An observer who cannot read ciphertext can still read its length. This\nmodule groups every plaintext into fixed buckets so the wire reveals\nonly a coarse size class instead of an exact byte count.\n\nWire format for one padded plaintext of bucket ``B``::\n\n    LENGTH_PREFIX || PLAINTEXT || RANDOM_PAD\n\nwhere ``LENGTH_PREFIX`` is the true plaintext length as a 4-byte\nbig-endian unsigned integer and ``RANDOM_PAD`` is fresh output from\n:mod:`secrets` filling the remainder ``B - prefix - len(plaintext)``.\nThe padded plaintext is then encrypted with AES-256-GCM, so the stored\nand transmitted ciphertext length is ``B + GCM_OVERHEAD_BYTES`` for\nevery plaintext inside the same bucket.\n\nCache safety contract: the only value ever cached is the immutable\nbucket table itself, keyed by configuration version, never by message\ncontent or message length. Padding bytes are drawn fresh from the\noperating-system CSPRNG on every call and are never stored, reused, or\nplaced in any cache. Reusing pad bytes across envelopes would make\nequal-length plaintexts produce related padded inputs, so reuse is\nforbidden by construction: there is no API that accepts caller-supplied\npad bytes and no cache entry that holds them.\n\nBucket lookup always scans the full table so the number of iterations\ndoes not depend on which bucket matched.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"","members":["utils/padding.py::LENGTH_PREFIX_BYTES","utils/padding.py::GCM_IV_BYTES","utils/padding.py::GCM_TAG_BYTES","utils/padding.py::GCM_OVERHEAD_BYTES","utils/padding.py::DEFAULT_MESSAGE_BUCKETS","utils/padding.py::DEFAULT_FILE_BUCKETS","utils/padding.py::MESSAGE_BUCKETS_ENV_VAR","utils/padding.py::FILE_BUCKETS_ENV_VAR","utils/padding.py::PaddingError","utils/padding.py::PaddingConfig","utils/padding.py::config_from_env","utils/padding.py::cached_tables","utils/padding.py::bucket_for","utils/padding.py::pad","utils/padding.py::unpad","utils/padding.py::wire_ciphertext_len","utils/padding.py::is_allowed_ciphertext_len"],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
